{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld","id":1553232,"title":"Forsaken in the Underworld?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-17T08:13:47-07:00","id":1553232,"title":"Forsaken in the Underworld?","content":"What are the limits to making a Werewolf character who scored the Underworld? <br /> <br /> Death gifts might be helpful for dealing with ghosts in the surface, could a pack bind a Geist as a totem? could they learn gifts from kerberoi/Geists and reapers? are there any lodges who go into detail with Werewolves going into the Underworld?<br /> <br /> If forced into the Underworld how would a l\u00edne wolf or pack survive? Or how long cold they survive?<br /> <br /> If gifts like Shadows Gaze don't work on ghosts (It says any spirit they can see, but ghosts are not spirits...) how would werewolves affect the dead? (I know I have seen some stuff about one Shadows using ghosts like most werewolves use spirits...)<br /> <br /> Would killing and eating ghosts give them essence and is there an issue with Harmony? Could they break towards something else (not human/spirit sides of themselves?) Hunting in the Underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T09:31:56-07:00","id":1553234,"title":"","content":"A geist is not a spirit and therefore any method of getting one as a totem is going to be unusual \u2014 they can only communicate and be communicated with in the context of fear and intimidation and they don't have the Essence concerns a spirit would have that makes becoming a totem an attractive offer.<br /> <br /> Kerberoi and Reapers are likewise not spirits and thus are not assumed to have the metaphysical qualities, knowledge, or anatomy needed to scar Gifts into werewolves.<br /> <br /> Book of the Dead is 1e and thus may require adaptation and judgment calls, but its section on various monsters in the Underworld is fairly comprehensive. Going from that\u2026<br /> <br /> Most rites that affect spirits don't affect ghosts, but rites that affect humans can.<br /> <br /> Werewolves of any quantity are going to run into the same survival problems as normal living people in the Underworld with the added wrinkle that eating ghosts has the same spiritual effects and consequences as eating humans.<br /> <br /> Werewolves who have an auspice may also find their spiritual nature adapting to the Underworld in a similar phenomenon to what makes them a probable origin of briarwolves in the Hedge (being border-dwelling shapeshifters whose border realm no longer exists), which 2e's low-Harmony confinement to the Shadow further echoes. There's a story hook that the totem of the Lodge of Death is rumored to enable its members to avoid this degeneration, and the Pure do not suffer it in the Underworld in particular (being separated from Luna's light and the support of the Lunes being non-issues for them), but the Great Below in general is of less concern to werewolves without specific drives and plenty of time to spare.<br /> <br /> In general, the dead require specialist knowledge to deal with, for which alliance and patronage from spirits of death is the most straightforward route.<br /> <br /> I don't know what you mean by &quot;scored the Underworld.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T13:45:21-07:00","id":1553236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553234#post1553234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A geist is not a spirit and therefore any method of getting one as a totem is going to be unusual \u2014 they can only communicate and be communicated with in the context of fear and intimidation and they don't have the Essence concerns a spirit would have that makes becoming a totem an attractive offer.<br /> <br /> Kerberoi and Reapers are likewise not spirits and thus are not assumed to have the metaphysical qualities, knowledge, or anatomy needed to scar Gifts into werewolves.<br /> <br /> Book of the Dead is 1e and thus may require adaptation and judgment calls, but its section on various monsters in the Underworld is fairly comprehensive. Going from that\u2026<br /> <br /> Most rites that affect spirits don't affect ghosts, but rites that affect humans can.<br /> <br /> Werewolves of any quantity are going to run into the same survival problems as normal living people in the Underworld with the added wrinkle that eating ghosts has the same spiritual effects and consequences as eating humans.<br /> <br /> Werewolves who have an auspice may also find their spiritual nature adapting to the Underworld in a similar phenomenon to what makes them a probable origin of briarwolves in the Hedge (being border-dwelling shapeshifters whose border realm no longer exists), which 2e's low-Harmony confinement to the Shadow further echoes. There's a story hook that the totem of the Lodge of Death is rumored to enable its members to avoid this degeneration, and the Pure do not suffer it in the Underworld in particular (being separated from Luna's light and the support of the Lunes being non-issues for them), but the Great Below in general is of less concern to werewolves without specific drives and plenty of time to spare.<br /> <br /> In general, the dead require specialist knowledge to deal with, for which alliance and patronage from spirits of death is the most straightforward route.<br /> <br /> I don't know what you mean by &quot;scored the Underworld.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what I meant by scored, it was a typo that I can't make much sense of.<br /> <br /> So the character I am thinking of (or pack?) would be forced into the Underworld, I was thinking of Death gifts, so they could see the dead and appear dead. But I'm not entirely sure either is useful in the Underworld. Some of the laws of deep dominions are suggested to state that the living don't belong, but I my brief reading of the Gift which hides your life signs seems to suggest nothing about it being more than a superficial physical change - enough to fool human eyes, but probably not Kerberoi?<br /> <br /> What build would you make for a Werewolf who was forced into the Underworld for them to survive there (and possibly thrive) what would they hunt (given that this is a main theme and drive for werewolves).<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of their spiritual nature adapting, I didn't know that was a thing... Also, Death wolf's ghost might be interesting. But I suspect conversations about a rank 7? Ghost have been done to death (no pun intended).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  typo 08-17-2025, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T13:48:29-07:00","id":1553237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553234#post1553234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know what you mean by &quot;scored the Underworld.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, although I may be wrong, that orathaic meant &quot;scoured&quot;.<br /> <br /> But I wonder if there could be specialized Gifts and Merits for Werewolves that deal with Ghosts and the Underworld in a regular basis, specially if they're trapped there for a long time. Not as in if those actually exist, but if making them would make sense, and how they would be. Maybe requiring help of a Death spirit, or indeed the unusual use of a Geist as a Totem.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I'm really curious to know the context of OP's hypothetical Werewolf and why specifically they need this kind of adaptation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T14:14:03-07:00","id":1553238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553237#post1553237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think, although I may be wrong, that orathaic meant &quot;scoured&quot;.<br /> <br /> But I wonder if there could be specialized Gifts and Merits for Werewolves that deal with Ghosts and the Underworld in a regular basis, specially if they're trapped there for a long time. Not as in if those actually exist, but if making them would make sense, and how they would be. Maybe requiring help of a Death spirit, or indeed the unusual use of a Geist as a Totem.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I'm really curious to know the context of OP's hypothetical Werewolf and why specifically they need this kind of adaptation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, generally I dislike the game. Something about Werewolf has never appealed to me. But I had a thought about a character which might appeal to me, and a specific context.<br /> <br /> I do like doing things which are a bit un-orthodox, and I was looking at Werewolf to see how I would build a character to best explore the Underworld... But I couldn't really come up with much. Infact it seems like the only advantage werewolves have over humans in the Underworld is being able to kill/eat ghosts to regain essence.<br /> <br /> Which still leaves their human-half hungry, I presume. [EDIT: this seems wrong, judging by the &quot;eating humans for essence&quot; rules for high Primal Urge, and counting ghosts as humans... Though Barghest seem more likely to count as animals...]<br /> <br /> Some of the Death gifts make it easier to deal with ghosts in deathly twilight, and to find an Avernian Gate, but that seems to be a single gift which does nothing in the Underworld (where ghosts are already visible by default).<br /> <br /> To your question, assume the Werewolf (or entire pack) is hiding from any enemy in the Underworld. Perhaps they will degenerate into unplayable antagonists, I see Book of the Dead suggests that lost werewolves may be one origin of Kerberoi. Which, yeah, that could be funky, but I do want something new.<br /> <br /> I would prefer to keep the hunting aspect, and if possible the pack (even if that means something different when you potentially have a different types of entity to as your totem).<br /> <br /> If you want particular details of the enemy, and why this is the best option, I had been working on the assumption that all the werewolves were dead. Even antagonistic werewolves who have become hunters in the Underworld would be sligthly more interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  typo 08-17-2025, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T16:28:40-07:00","id":1553239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553238#post1553238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, generally I dislike the game. Something about Werewolf has never appealed to me. But I had a thought about a character which might appeal to me, and a specific context.<br /> <br /> I do like doing things which are a bit un-orthodox, and I was looking at Werewolf to see how I would build a character to best explore the Underworld... But I couldn't really come up with much. Infact it seems like the only advantage werewolves have over humans in the Underworld is being able to kill/eat ghosts to regain essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be because, as pretty much every monster type tied to an otherworld demonstrates by comparison with mortals, things that aren't the Bound need specialized tools or specific tricks to access the Underworld and do not generally get special benefits to operating in it, and werewolves are not naturally specialized to deal with the Underworld except as part of a failstate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To your question, assume the Werewolf (or entire pack) is hiding from any enemy in the Underworld. Perhaps they will degenerate into unplayable antagonists, I see Book of the Dead suggests that lost werewolves may be one origin of Kerberoi. Which, yeah, that could be funky, but I do want something new. </div> </div> </div>The Shadow and the material world are generally going to be much more suited for werewolves to hide from enemies unless they've screwed things up to a nigh-unthinkable degree, between the complexity of political games in the Shadow and the thickness of the Gauntlet roughly corresponding to population density (to say nothing of their natural toolkit working within those spheres).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would prefer to keep the hunting aspect, and if possible the pack (even if that means something different when you potentially have a different types of entity to as your totem).<br /> <br /> If you want particular details of the enemy, and why this is the best option, I had been working on the assumption that all the werewolves were dead. Even antagonistic werewolves who have become hunters in the Underworld would be sligthly more interesting... </div> </div> </div>It is worth pointing out that Book of the Dead also notes that, whatever happens to werewolves' spirits after death, they're not leaving ghosts that descend to the Underworld in normal circumstances.<br /> <br /> It is also worth pointing out that the Underworld in 2e is overall less conducive to naturalized hunters since the world itself is an ambush predator and most of its proactive efforts are tilted toward dragging new food in from the land of the living or introducing destabilizing elements to its most stable communities; if a werewolf pack is hunting in the Underworld it's because they're looking for something, same as anywhere else.<br /> <br /> Setting aside the iffy nature of trying to build support for a concept that's trying to be different for its own sake, I have to ask why you're bothering with a game that doesn't appeal to you in the first place, much less trying to bend it toward what seems to be not only refocusing its tools toward a completely different otherworld but apparently making that otherworld the primary play-location over the material world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T16:38:29-07:00","id":1553240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553238#post1553238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I couldn't really come up with much. Infact it seems like the only advantage werewolves have over humans in the Underworld is being able to kill/eat ghosts to regain essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>For starters, I can't verify in the book right now, but I think that eating in the realm proper would still nourish them. IIRC that's how a Werewolf can survive in the Shadow, where everything is Ephemera.<br /> <br /> But that aside, power itself is the main disadvantage for humans in the Underworld. Food is something you can bring from outside, and while definitely not living, Ghosts are far easier to interact with than Spirits, <i>specially</i> in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> So I would first look into how a pack can adapt through mundane means. Living in the underworld doesn't have to be exclusive, so they may travel outside from time to time to forage for resources, either in the Material World or the Shadow (for things like Gifts), and then go back to their affairs in the Underworld<br /> <br /> IIRC they can also get things within or for cities in the Underworld, whether in the Autochthonous Depths, at River Cities, or in some Dead Dominions, so both buying and foraging in the cities is possible, and getting stuff by doing services to those cities. Death spirits also frequent the Underworld, as strongly Death-resonant places within the Shadow have natural, always open caves to the Underworld, so there are both spirits still to deal with and passage to and from the Shadow without going through the Material (or necessarily through the Upper Reaches) if this is a concern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553238#post1553238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps they will degenerate into unplayable antagonists</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but I think with enough effort it is doable even without specialized traits, which is also still doable.<br /> <br /> For your particular take, I think making up your own rules for a few things may be worth the try. Some may be Merits or Gifts, but some may be straight-up changes to how Werewolves operate, simply because that would be a particular, different group of Werewolves, for a particular, different chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553238#post1553238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would prefer to keep the hunting aspect, and if possible the pack (even if that means something different when you potentially have a different types of entity to as your totem).</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest problem with getting a Geist as a Totem would just be to adjust what the entity gets out of the deal. Also, a Pack isn't just defined by a Totem, but also by Pack Rites, which still work as normal. On top of that, IIRC there are no rules against letting Ghosts joint the Pack, and it may be enough to shake things a lot without much rule-changing.<br /> <br /> On the hunting aspect, as a theme it isn't a problem at all, you just have to ponder the kinds of prey Werewolves have access to in the Underworld. I believe most Hunter's Aspects won't need much in terms of tweaking. What may need heavy modification are the Tribes' preferred prey and benefits for Siskur-Dah. You may have to jot down as many categories of prey as you can, just to see which ways of defining them works better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553238#post1553238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even antagonistic werewolves who have become hunters in the Underworld would be sligthly more interesting...</div> </div> </div> </div>In a sense, your goal is to make a new kind of Werewolf and ditch the original game altogether. If this is the case, I wouldn't so much think about how to build an Underworld-dwelling Werewolf within the constraints of the game as is, as that would mean using the full power of a splat to make a limited build similar to any static monster stat block. Instead, I would focus on making the whole concept work within the Underworld instead, with all variety it brings with it (and of course, in the way to require the minimum effort, but still a complete adaptation).<br /> <br /> So don't worry about what does exist in canon that let a Werewolf live in the Underworld, and instead look at what you think Werewolves need to live in the Underworld and just give it to them. You can justify whatever result you get as them adapting after having to flee the Shadow for whatever reason you want (if not always dwelling there to begin with).<br /> <br /> Other than that, then you're probably better with a single pack that pulls it off through the usual resources and a specialized organization (as opposed to a specialized power set), or with a simpler stat block for an Underworld-based &quot;werewolf&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T16:52:13-07:00","id":1553241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Setting aside the iffy nature of trying to build support for a concept that's trying to be different for its own sake, I have to ask why you're bothering with a game that doesn't appeal to you in the first place, much less trying to bend it toward what seems to be not only refocusing its tools toward a completely different otherworld but apparently making that otherworld the primary play-location over the material world. </div> </div> </div>Well originally I wasn't, my plan was to just say all the werewolves were dead. <br /> <br /> But, in case I didn't already say, I like doing things that I find interesting - taking werewolves and making them do something they are not designed for and seeing what 'would' happen, is pretty interesting to me.<br /> <br /> If you need more of a reason than that, I can suggest the Magic the Gathering player types ( psychographic profile).<br /> <br /> The why is just what I said above, I played magic as a Johnny/Jenny type, doing weird combos for the sake it. Trying to <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Johnny may be a player who seeks niche cards, or cards widely reputed as bad, and tries to &quot;break&quot; them, exploiting them in ways to give abnormal power and win the game. </div> </div> </div>This is unnecessary, but it is what I enjoy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553239#post1553239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be because, as pretty much every monster type tied to an otherworld demonstrates by comparison with mortals, things that aren't the Bound need specialized tools or specific tricks to access the Underworld and do not generally get special benefits to operating in it, and werewolves are not naturally specialized to deal with the Underworld except as part of a failstate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can acknowledge that, but I am pretty sure despite having an affinity for the hedge, changeling has hell-divers who can more easily enter the Underworld, Promethean has the Ulgan, etc. <br /> <br /> The Bone Shadows seem the most likely to have some Underworld knowledge...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Shadow and the material world are generally going to be much more suited for werewolves to hide from enemies unless they've screwed things up to a nigh-unthinkable degree, between the complexity of political games in the Shadow and the thickness of the Gauntlet roughly corresponding to population density (to say nothing of their natural toolkit working within those spheres). </div> </div> </div> yes, I am fairly sure that assuming all other werewolves are dead, things have been screened up to a nigh-unthinkable degree. Staying in the Shadow might be an alternative option, but it is the first place you would look, and losing all harmony there, to the point where you can't leave is less interesting to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is worth pointing out that Book of the Dead also notes that, whatever happens to werewolves' spirits after death, they're not leaving ghosts that descend to the Underworld in normal circumstances.<br /> <br /> It is also worth pointing out that the Underworld in 2e is overall less conducive to naturalized hunters since the world itself is an ambush predator and most of its proactive efforts are tilted toward dragging new food in from the land of the living or introducing destabilizing elements to its most stable communities; if a werewolf pack is hunting in the Underworld it's because they're looking for something, same as anywhere else. </div> </div> </div>I suppose the Underworld of 2e taking Werewolves and using them as a tool would be in-line with its goals, Reapers are used to further the goals of the Underworld, so I don't see Werewolves becoming more like Underworld natives via making some abhorent deal being less reasonable. <br /> <br /> That give some some ideas, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T17:59:45-07:00","id":1553243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553241#post1553241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I can acknowledge that, but I am pretty sure despite having an affinity for the hedge, changeling has hell-divers who can more easily enter the Underworld, Promethean has the Ulgan, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Helldivers get the ability to open otherworldly gates and be better at Larceny in other worlds. Ulgans get to interact with ghostly and spiritual Twilight and Prometheans in general come back from death by a vignette in the Underworld. Both of these are different things from being able to sustain oneself on food that only sustains the dead or the fae or innately speaking the universal language of the Shadow or always knowing which Astral route to take to reach a specific Lair, and replicating the full survival kit of a half-native as a different monster type is generally several steps of kit-assembly.<br /> <br /> Mages can get away with approaching this relatively quickly by virtue of the way the Arcana work and the thematic notion of its PCs having the tools to get in over their heads, but anything that doesn't have a full improvisational powerset at its fingertips has to take Merits, rituals, and other powers to replicate a sizeable portion of another splat's template features or make peace with there being gaps in the safety suite for engaging with an environment that is at best neutrally-inclined toward human life and more often directly hostile to survival therein.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Bone Shadows seem the most likely to have some Underworld knowledge... </div> </div> </div>The Lodge of Death, one of the three Pillars of the Bone Shadows, are known to probe the mysteries of death and thus may have additional knowledge of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> yes, I am fairly sure that assuming all other werewolves are dead, things have been screened up to a nigh-unthinkable degree. Staying in the Shadow might be an alternative option, but it is the first place you would look, and losing all harmony there, to the point where you can't leave is less interesting to me. </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Shadow is the first place you'd look&quot; is the equivalent of saying that if someone has done something to get federal law enforcement on their tail the first place they should look is The Planet Earth, and I'm now confused about whether you're saying that the entire werewolf pack this hypothetical game concerns is dead or that in this proposition <i>every</i> werewolf is dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose the Underworld of 2e taking Werewolves and using them as a tool would be in-line with its goals, Reapers are used to further the goals of the Underworld, so I don't see Werewolves becoming more like Underworld natives via making some abhorent deal being less reasonable. </div> </div> </div>Reapers become what they are by the Underworld &quot;offering&quot; them a deathmask, which applies its effects to ghosts to &quot;become&quot; a specific Reaper per deathmask, which notably does not happen to the Bound despite their closeness to the state of actual ghostliness. Meanwhile, the &quot;true natives&quot; of the Underworld prop living-world Avernian Gates open and rapidly perish outside of the Underworld except in the area of a Gate.<br /> <br /> If you want to try a game where the PCs are Reapers with an unusual set of extra Numina nobody's stopping you, but if you intend to use mostly the normal Werewolf mechanics to play a game set in the Underworld you're firmly in the realm of full homebrew rather than any kind of niche interaction. Ghosts and the Underworld are more specific than the breadth of Weird Shit the Shadow can bring into the narrative; a pack of Ghost Wolves with an extremely powerful pack totem and/or lodge totem from the choirs of death might grant esoteric abilities to learn Gifts by consuming Mementos, glean the symbolism for rites from tableaux, develop unusual new Merits to refine their forms by drinking from the Rivers, or exchange their auspice for stranger powers at the Ocean of Fragments, but &quot;what are the limits of the printed material?&quot; is a bit of a silly question when that boils down to &quot;werewolves are not made for the Underworld&quot; and &quot;if you are willing to put in the work, you can contrive a circumstance for just about anything to happen.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T19:28:13-07:00","id":1553246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553241#post1553241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I can acknowledge that, but I am pretty sure despite having an affinity for the hedge, changeling has hell-divers who can more easily enter the Underworld, Promethean has the Ulgan, etc.<br /> <br /> The Bone Shadows seem the most likely to have some Underworld knowledge...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Those examples have less to do with &quot;those splats can live in the Underworld&quot;, and more to do with &quot;they have basic awareness of the Underworld and some means to get there&quot;. Which Werewolves also have, through the Shadow Caves where Death-Spirits dwell.<br /> <br /> None of them actually have any means of sustenance or long-term permanence in the Underworld beyond what any mortal human has.<br /> <br /> And this isn't a problem. Compared to the Shadow or the Hedge, the Underworld is remarkably hospitable for humans, it isn't intrinsically harder to explore than any other cave complex. You need supplies, but that's it. Even the inhabitants are less frequently hostile (although still quite dangerous).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T21:03:39-07:00","id":1553249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553243#post1553243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;snip&gt; but anything that doesn't have a full improvisational powerset at its fingertips has to take Merits, rituals, and other powers to replicate a sizeable portion of another splat's template features or make peace with there being gaps in the safety suite for engaging with an environment that is at best neutrally-inclined toward human life and more often directly hostile to survival therein.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what merits or rituals would help, I guess that remains my question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lodge of Death, one of the three Pillars of the Bone Shadows, are known to probe the mysteries of death and thus may have additional knowledge of the Underworld. </div> </div> </div>I will have to read more about theodge of Death.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The Shadow is the first place you'd look&quot; is the equivalent of saying that if someone has done something to get federal law enforcement on their tail the first place they should look is The Planet Earth, and I'm now confused about whether you're saying that the entire werewolf pack this hypothetical game concerns is dead or that in this proposition <i>every</i> werewolf is dead. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is every other Werewolf is dead.<br /> <br /> Except the one pack who figured out how to survive in the Underworld... And yes, depending on who or what is killing werewolves, the Shadow is going to be a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &lt;snip&gt; a pack of Ghost Wolves with an extremely powerful pack totem and/or lodge totem from the choirs of death might grant esoteric abilities to learn Gifts by consuming Mementos, glean the symbolism for rites from tableaux, develop unusual new Merits to refine their forms by drinking from the Rivers, or exchange their auspice for stranger powers at the Ocean of Fragments, but &quot;what are the limits of the printed material?&quot; is a bit of a silly question when that boils down to &quot;werewolves are not made for the Underworld&quot; and &quot;if you are willing to put in the work, you can contrive a circumstance for just about anything to happen.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Why Ghost wovles and not Bone Shadows? I know the one advantage Bone Shadows have is Death Gifts granted by their tribal totem, which, while not exactly much help, is still a step above having no tribe.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;Find a powerful totem spirit from the choir of death, learn so esoteric abilities, and homebrew the effects of drinking from the rivers of the Underworld/surviving on Ectoplasmic ghosts&quot; would have been a much shorter answer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T22:49:04-07:00","id":1553250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553249#post1553249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what merits or rituals would help, I guess that remains my question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the things you are asking for do not already exist.<br /> <br /> The rite in Book of the Dead provides an example in 1e Werewolf's formatting, which you may attempt to translate into 2e's systems for how rites work, for werewolves to try to cross between the lands of the living and the dead without engaging with the systems presented in Geist 2e instead. That is largely the extent of published material for werewolves to deal with the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Merits are this franchise's general-purpose mechanic for making granular tweaks to the way a character interacts with the world in the absence of a more specially-made mechanic, but there are not published Merits for acclimating werewolves and their powers to the Underworld, because Werewolf is not a game about delving into the Underworld and its characters are not built with the assumption that this is a thing they would need to do. You might take inspiration from the Ivory Claw Merits and Predator King Merits in Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon for the dot values accorded to certain types of effect, but you would still need to actually devise those Merits.<br /> <br /> You are asking what tools you can use for this and the answer is homebrew, which is best built for a purpose. There are no Johnny/Jenny MTG combo shenanigans to be had here. This is storytelling in a setting where the typical state of things is fairly well-delineated and weird exceptions occur often enough to dedicate a common title to the books collecting and debuting them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why Ghost wovles and not Bone Shadows? I know the one advantage Bone Shadows have is Death Gifts granted by their tribal totem, which, while not exactly much help, is still a step above having no tribe. </div> </div> </div>Because Ghost Wolves are the go-to population for having weird shit done to their template, as demonstrated by the number of variants in Shunned by the Moon that the Thihirtha Numea specifically are susceptible to, attempting to become equal in strength to a tribe is an easily defined ambition for lodge totems, and the Firstborn don't usually play quite as loose with what they can grant their adoptive progeny. If you want to enforce tribal membership in this hypothetical instead and/or grapple with e.g. the consequences of tribal patronage from a ghost-Firstborn then you're free to do so, but these are decisions you will have to make yourself to suit the story you're trying to facilitate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, &quot;Find a powerful totem spirit from the choir of death, learn so esoteric abilities, and homebrew the effects of drinking from the rivers of the Underworld/surviving on Ectoplasmic ghosts&quot; would have been a much shorter answer. </div> </div> </div>And &quot;I want help homebrewing for this very specific chronicle conceit&quot; would be a much more effective way of soliciting aid than asking what tools exist for a chronicle conceit that completely reorients werewolves from their normal place in the cosmology when most gamelines not named Mage or Beast only really give tools for using their related otherworld to the semi-natives the gameline concerns and maybe a more reliable means of entry than mortals get to other monsters if they have space.<br /> <br /> The amount of special rules werewolves have for interacting with the Underworld fits entirely into their section of Book of the Dead, which is from the previous edition. Literally everything else is going to have to be homebrew, because the Underworld was extremely mysterious and largely only speculatively described before Geist came out and then was notably reoriented in 2e when Geist came out again. Werewolves mainly hunt within territories and most things that are dead are not pursued into the lands of the dead unless they crawl back up into that territory, with the typical exceptions being dedicated specialists seeking deep lore beyond the scope of a typical pack hunter.<br /> <br /> If what you want is a general overview of how werewolves work I can provide that for you too, but it doesn't inspire confidence or motivate me to learn that you couldn't figure out &quot;I'll need to homebrew something to suit my needs&quot; from the starting premise of &quot;I want to run a game where the pack is the only surviving werewolves in the world, hiding out in the Underworld and adapting their spiritual nature to suit a place that absorbs forgotten ghosts into the walls instead of dealing with spirit politics in the primal reflections of material locations.&quot; Chronicles has not been written with crossover play specifically in mind for half its lifetime, most of its otherworlds are written as places you should be wary of lingering in, and werewolves have long been the primary window into the diverse ways in which the Shadow can bring strange trouble to bear as an extension of how spirits and resonance can do strange things even as they mistake non-spiritual phenomena for rare things within their area of expertise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-18T02:25:39-07:00","id":1553253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1553232-forsaken-in-the-underworld?p=1553250#post1553250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And &quot;I want help homebrewing for this very specific chronicle conceit&quot; would be a much more effective way of soliciting aid than asking what tools exist for ...</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to have almost gotten it.<br /> <br /> I didn't want help homebrewing, I wanted help knowing what was already written. <br /> <br /> And you have helped, I didn't know about that section of Book of the Dead, or how limited the gifts and rites presented in other places was.<br /> <br /> I also didn't know that werewolves with an Auspice would become mutated somehow by being away from the moon.<br /> <br /> But Johnny/Jenny style play isn't &quot;make up whatever card you want&quot; it is &quot;make the most interesting effect from the tools at your disposal&quot; - I wasn't asking about homebrew, because that is the last step I would want. And what while I am more than comfortable homebrewing for Mage, I don't know enough about Werewolf to start... <br /> <br /> Homebrewing needs a basic understanding of the systems you are tweaking. Which I clearly have some gaps in when it comes to Forsaken.<br /> <br /> I feel hunting a Chthonic being would be rather enjoyable plot points for a Werewolf game, I'm surprised there is almost nothing to work with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-25T19:39:27-07:00","id":1553451,"title":"","content":"One of the writer/developers for Werewolf the Forsaken did give an example of a pack with a ghost totem, the Hangmen. The books do call out that some packs have strange entities for totems, but the rules for them wouldn't be anything universal so would heavily depend upon the context of the wolves and totem entity involved, whatever it was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1235915-example-of-an-unusual-totem-the-hangmen\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1235915-example-of-an-unusual-totem-the-hangmen\"> [Example of an unusual totem] The Hangmen - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1235915-example-of-an-unusual-totem-the-hangmen\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1235915-example-of-an-unusual-totem-the-hangmen </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Hangmen The world is a place of blurred lines, filled with strange exceptions to every would-be law laid down by those attempting to bind reality with categories and clear distinctions. Most Uratha wouldn&rsquo;t bother to spare a moment&rsquo;s thought for the idea that beings other than spirits of the Shadow might slither into the shape and space of a pack&rsquo;s totem and bind werewolves together in sacred union. After all, generally, they can&rsquo;t. It isn&rsquo;t possible for a pack to seize any old ghost or phantasm in their talons and weave its essence into their bond &ndash; such an attempt will simply fail. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In the Dark Eras 2 book, the section on the Great War crosses over Werewolf, Geist, and Promethean. There's not much in the way of hard rules there but the ghost of Death Wolf is a major antagonist for the werewolves and there's a sidebar about geist totems on p417.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}